module contract;

// Card OPENSSL-PROVIDER-REMAINING-CALLEES. The SSL connection: handshake,
// I/O, its error code and what it carries (see err.qv for what every
// declaration of this crate shares).
//
// The handshake and I/O calls may run callbacks the SSL object or its
// SSL_CTX carries. Card OPENSSL-SSL-CTX-CALLBACK-SLOTS: the certificate
// callback is a stated invocation of the opaque slot `ssl_ctx_st.cert_cb`
// (C04.19.3, rule 12n), decided over the run's closed set of what its two
// declared setters are handed. SSL_set_cert_cb writes the SSL's own copy and
// SSL_new copies its context's ("The new structure inherits the settings of
// the underlying context", SSL_new, 3.5), so the SSL's slot holds a value one
// of the two setters was handed (or none): the two share one key, whose set
// is every value either can hold. The page (SSL_CTX_set_cert_cb, 3.5): it "is
// called before a certificate will be used by a client or server", with the
// connection and `arg` ("The callback can then inspect the passed ssl
// structure"), and "The next call to the handshake function will again lead
// to the call of cert_cb". The I/O calls run the handshake when needed
// ("If necessary, a read function will negotiate a TLS/SSL session", SSL_read
// 3.5; likewise SSL_write) and renegotiate on request.
//
// Card OPENSSL-UNSTATED-CALLBACK-SLOTS: the other slots a handshake runs are
// stated too, each with every writer its 3.5 page names declared as its
// setter (ssl_ctx.qv and below), and each read through one key shared by the
// context's slot and the SSL's copy:
//
// * the verify callback, `verify_callback(preverify_ok, x509_ctx)`
//   (SSL_CTX_set_verify, 3.5), `ssl_ctx_st.verify_callback`;
// * the info callback, "called whenever a significant event occurs such as:
//   the state changes, an alert appears, or an error occurs", as
//   `callback(SSL *ssl, int where, int ret)` (SSL_CTX_set_info_callback,
//   3.5), `ssl_ctx_st.info_callback`;
// * the message callback, for "all SSL/TLS/QUIC protocol messages (such as
//   handshake messages) that are received or sent", whose `ssl` is "The SSL
//   object that received or sent the message" (SSL_CTX_set_msg_callback,
//   3.5), `ssl_ctx_st.msg_callback`;
// * the security callback, "consulted whenever the library needs to decide
//   whether an algorithm, key, parameter or protocol version meets the
//   configured security level", where "checks originating from a connection
//   pass s (with ctx NULL)" (SSL_CTX_set_security_level, 3.5),
//   `ssl_ctx_st.sec_cb`;
// * the session callbacks (SSL_CTX_sess_set_get_cb, 3.5): `new_session_cb`
//   "passed the ssl connection and the nascent ssl session" (in TLSv1.3
//   "after the handshake", so during the I/O calls), `remove_session_cb`
//   "passed the ctx and the ssl session" (the session's context, not a
//   parameter here) and `get_session_cb` "passed the ssl connection and the
//   session id";
// * the client certificate callback, "called when a client certificate is
//   requested by a server", `client_cert_cb(SSL *ssl, X509 **x509, EVP_PKEY
//   **pkey)` (SSL_CTX_set_client_cert_cb, 3.5).
//
// Card OPENSSL-UNDECLARED-HANDSHAKE-CALLBACKS: and the handshake slots whose
// setters ssl_handshake.qv now declares, each with every writer its 3.5 page
// names:
//
// * the keylog callback, "called whenever TLS key material is generated or
//   received" with "the ssl object associated with the connection, and
//   line" (SSL_CTX_set_keylog_callback), `ssl_ctx_st.keylog_callback`;
// * the ALPN selection callback, `cb(ssl, out, outlen, in, inlen, arg)` "used
//   by a server to select which protocol to use for the incoming
//   connection", and the NPN selection and advertisement callbacks of the
//   same page (SSL_CTX_set_alpn_select_cb), `ssl_ctx_st.alpn_select_cb`,
//   `.npn_select_cb`, `.npn_advertised_cb`;
// * the certificate verification callback, "called instead with the
//   arguments callback(X509_STORE_CTX *x509_store_ctx, void *arg)" when "a
//   peer certificate has been received during an SSL/TLS handshake"
//   (SSL_CTX_set_cert_verify_callback), `ssl_ctx_st.app_verify_callback`;
// * the PSK callbacks, each "given the connection in parameter ssl"
//   (SSL_CTX_set_psk_client_callback, SSL_CTX_use_psk_identity_hint),
//   `.psk_client_callback`, `.psk_use_session_cb`, `.psk_server_callback`,
//   `.psk_find_session_cb`;
// * the ClientHello callback, "called during the early stages of ClientHello
//   processing on the server" (SSL_CTX_set_client_hello_cb),
//   `.client_hello_cb`;
// * the record padding callback, "invoked for every record before
//   encryption" (SSL_CTX_set_record_padding_callback), `.record_padding_cb`;
// * the early data callback, "called at a point in the handshake immediately
//   before a decision is made to accept or reject early data"
//   (SSL_read_early_data), `.allow_early_data_cb`;
// * the custom extension callbacks, add_cb "called to send custom extension
//   data", free_cb "with the value of out set by the add callback", parse_cb
//   "receives data for TLS extensions", in both callback styles
//   (SSL_extension_supported), `.custom_ext_add_cb_ex` and its five
//   siblings.
//
// Card OPENSSL-BIO-METHODS-AND-CALLBACKS: and the slots of the BIOs the SSL
// object holds (bio_slots.qv), through which every record is written and
// read: the BIO's callback, "called during most high-level BIO operations"
// (BIO_set_callback, 3.5), `bio_st.bio_callback_ex` and `bio_st.bio_callback`; and
// each function of its method table, called "in response to" the BIO
// operation it implements (BIO_meth_new, 3.5), `bio_method_st.meth_write_ex`,
// `.meth_write`, `.meth_read_ex`, `.meth_read`, `.meth_puts`, `.meth_gets`, `.meth_ctrl`,
// `.meth_create`, `.meth_destroy`, `.meth_callback_ctrl`, `.meth_sendmmsg`, `.meth_recvmmsg`. The
// SSL pages do not say which BIO operations the record layer performs, so
// every one is stated (stating more never improves a verdict). Each is
// handed the BIO, never the connection, so every actual is `_`. The keys are
// run-wide: the set is every function any setter is handed, beside the
// methods the library defines itself (BIO_s_socket, BIO_s_mem, ...), which no
// setter is handed and which the library-value premise
// `openssl_builtin_bio_methods` (C04.18) covers.
//
// Card OPENSSL-REMAINING-HANDSHAKE-SETTERS: and the remaining slots whose
// setters ssl_handshake_setters.qv and x509_store_slots.qv now declare:
//
// * the session ticket callbacks, gen_cb "invoked when a session ticket is
//   about to be created" and dec_cb "invoked after session ticket decryption
//   has been attempted" (SSL_CTX_set_session_ticket_cb),
//   `ssl_ctx_st.ticket_gen_cb`, `.ticket_dec_cb`;
// * the session id generator, called "When a new session is established"
//   on the server (SSL_CTX_set_generate_session_id),
//   `.generate_session_id`;
// * the DH parameter callback, "invoked during a connection when DH
//   parameters are required" with "The SSL object for the current
//   connection" (SSL_CTX_set_tmp_dh_callback), `.tmp_dh_callback`;
// * the stateless TLS 1.3 and the DTLS cookie callbacks, whose zero return
//   "can be used to abort the handshake"
//   (SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb), `.gen_stateless_cookie_cb`,
//   `.verify_stateless_cookie_cb`, `.app_gen_cookie_cb`,
//   `.app_verify_cookie_cb`. The page names SSL_stateless and DTLSv1_listen
//   as their users, neither declared; stating them on the handshake also
//   covers a DTLS server handshake with cookie exchange (stating more never
//   improves a verdict);
// * the session secret callback, whose `peer_ciphers` "On the client side
//   ... will always be NULL" (SSL_set_session_secret_cb),
//   `ssl_st.session_secret_cb`;
// * the SRP callbacks, each given "the SSL connection s"
//   (SSL_CTX_set_srp_password), `.srp_username_callback`,
//   `.srp_client_pwd_callback`, `.srp_verify_param_callback`;
// * the async callback, called when, during "an asynchronous SSL call", "a
//   retry occurs" (SSL_set_async_callback), `.async_cb`;
// * the QUIC pending connection callback, run as "TLS handshake processing
//   may occur independently from the thread which accepts the connection"
//   (SSL_CTX_set_new_pending_conn_cb), `.new_pending_conn_cb`, every actual
//   the library's (the listener's context and a preallocated connection);
// * the twelve callbacks of a certificate store, which "are inherited by the
//   corresponding X509_STORE_CTX structure when it is initialized"
//   (X509_STORE_set_verify_cb_func), run by the verification of the peer's
//   chain, `x509_store_st.verify_cb` and its eleven siblings, every actual
//   the library's.
//
// Two invocations the vocabulary cannot place on a call are not stated by
// any declaration: the async callback run later by the engine "via a
// polling mechanism or via an interrupt", and the QUIC callbacks run by a
// QUIC thread outside any call. The report records them.
//
// What each callback hands back (a session reference a new-session callback
// keeps by returning 1, the certificate and key a client certificate
// callback sets, the password an SRP client callback returns, which the
// library frees, the issuer a store's get_issuer must up-ref) is outside
// C04.19's identity composition, so a run that registers such a callback
// refuses these calls; one that registers none, or only identity candidates,
// decides them. What these calls may still run unstated (an
// SSL_CTX_callback_ctrl arm: the servername, status or ticket key callback;
// the certificate transparency validation callback, which SSL_CTX_enable_ct
// writes with the library's own; the not-resumable session and session
// ticket extension callbacks, whose setters no manual page documents; a
// function of the lookup methods the context's store holds; an ex_data
// callback)
// stays under the narrowed premise
// `openssl_unstated_callback_slots` (C04.18), published with every row that
// applies these declarations. The callbacks themselves are the application's
// functions, analysed on their own rows.

// SSL_write: https://docs.openssl.org/1.0.2/man3/SSL_write/ (also 3.5,
// 1.1.1). HISTORY (3.5) names only SSL_write_ex(), SSL_sendfile() and
// SSL_write_ex2(), so the bound is the oldest series that documents
// SSL_write. DESCRIPTION (3.5): it "write[s] num bytes from the buffer buf
// into the specified ssl connection". A retried write must be repeated
// "with the same arguments" (NOTES): a protocol on the caller, not a
// retention of `buf`. Pinned prototype: `int SSL_write(SSL *ssl, const void
// *buf, int num)` (openssl/ssl.h).
// Card OPENSSL-EX-DATA-REGISTRY: a handshake run by the call creates and
// frees sessions, peer certificates and keys.
extern fn SSL_write(ssl: ptr<mut, u8>, buf: ptr<const, u8>, num: i32) -> i32
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    requires resource_revision(flexible);
    requires resource_library_version(openssl, documented "1.0.2");
    requires resource_premise(openssl_unstated_callback_slots,
        #slots(#of(SSL, #args) | #ctx(#of(SSL, #args)) | #of(SSL_CTX, #args)) \ #stated |-> #inert
        && (quant all #l in #lookups(#store(#ctx(#of(SSL, #args)) | #of(SSL_CTX, #args))): #fns(#l) \ #stated |-> #inert)
        && quant all #o in #created | #copied | #freed: #ex_data(#class(#o)) \ #stated |-> #inert);
    requires resource_premise(openssl_builtin_bio_methods,
        quant all #b in #chain(#of(BIO, #args) | #bios(#of(SSL, #args))): #method(#b) in #builtin
        -> #fns(#b) |-> #inert
        && quant all #f in #fns(#b): #in_turn(#f, #ssl_of(#b) \ #args) |-> #inert);
    requires resource_premise(openssl_ex_data_callbacks,
        quant all #o in #created | #copied | #freed: #ex_data(#class(#o)) |-> #inert);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(ssl);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(buf);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(num);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.cert_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.verify_callback, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.info_callback, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.msg_callback, _, _, _, _, _, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.sec_cb, ssl, supplied_nullable, _, _, _, supplied_nullable, supplied_nullable);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.new_session_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.remove_session_cb, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.get_session_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.client_cert_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.keylog_callback, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.alpn_select_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.npn_select_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.npn_advertised_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.app_verify_callback, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_client_callback, ssl, supplied_nullable, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_use_session_cb, ssl, supplied_nullable, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_server_callback, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_find_session_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.client_hello_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.record_padding_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.allow_early_data_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_add_cb_ex, ssl, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_free_cb_ex, ssl, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_parse_cb_ex, ssl, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_add_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_free_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_parse_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.ticket_gen_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.ticket_dec_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.generate_session_id, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.tmp_dh_callback, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.gen_stateless_cookie_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.verify_stateless_cookie_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.app_gen_cookie_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.app_verify_cookie_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_st.session_secret_cb, ssl, _, _, supplied_nullable, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.srp_username_callback, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.srp_client_pwd_callback, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.srp_verify_param_callback, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.async_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.new_pending_conn_cb, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.verify_cb, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.verify, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.get_issuer, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.check_issued, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.check_revocation, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.get_crl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.check_crl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.cert_crl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.check_policy, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.lookup_certs, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.lookup_crls, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, x509_store_st.cleanup_fn, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_st.bio_callback_ex, _, _, supplied_nullable, _, _, _, _, supplied_nullable);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_st.bio_callback, _, _, supplied_nullable, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_write_ex, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_write, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_read_ex, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_read, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_puts, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_gets, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_ctrl, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_create, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_destroy, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_callback_ctrl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_sendmmsg, _, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, bio_method_st.meth_recvmmsg, _, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

// SSL_read: https://docs.openssl.org/1.0.2/man3/SSL_read/ (also 3.5,
// 1.1.1). HISTORY (3.5) names only SSL_read_ex() and SSL_peek_ex().
// DESCRIPTION (3.5): it tries "to read num bytes from the specified ssl into
// the buffer buf". Pinned prototype: `int SSL_read(SSL *ssl, void *buf, int
// num)`.
// Card OPENSSL-EX-DATA-REGISTRY: a handshake run by the call creates and
// frees sessions, peer certificates and keys.
extern fn SSL_read(ssl: ptr<mut, u8>, buf: ptr<mut, u8>, num: i32) -> i32
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    requires resource_revision(flexible);
    requires resource_library_version(openssl, documented "1.0.2");
    requires resource_premise(openssl_unstated_callback_slots,
        #slots(#of(SSL, #args) | #ctx(#of(SSL, #args)) | #of(SSL_CTX, #args)) \ #stated |-> #inert
        && (quant all #l in #lookups(#store(#ctx(#of(SSL, #args)) | #of(SSL_CTX, #args))): #fns(#l) \ #stated |-> #inert)
        && quant all #o in #created | #copied | #freed: #ex_data(#class(#o)) \ #stated |-> #inert);
    requires resource_premise(openssl_builtin_bio_methods,
        quant all #b in #chain(#of(BIO, #args) | #bios(#of(SSL, #args))): #method(#b) in #builtin
        -> #fns(#b) |-> #inert
        && quant all #f in #fns(#b): #in_turn(#f, #ssl_of(#b) \ #args) |-> #inert);
    requires resource_premise(openssl_ex_data_callbacks,
        quant all #o in #created | #copied | #freed: #ex_data(#class(#o)) |-> #inert);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(ssl);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(buf);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(num);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.cert_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.verify_callback, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.info_callback, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.msg_callback, _, _, _, _, _, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.sec_cb, ssl, supplied_nullable, _, _, _, supplied_nullable, supplied_nullable);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.new_session_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.remove_session_cb, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.get_session_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.client_cert_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.keylog_callback, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.alpn_select_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.npn_select_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.npn_advertised_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.app_verify_callback, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_client_callback, ssl, supplied_nullable, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_use_session_cb, ssl, supplied_nullable, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_server_callback, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.psk_find_session_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.client_hello_cb, ssl, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.record_padding_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.allow_early_data_cb, ssl, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_add_cb_ex, ssl, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_free_cb_ex, ssl, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_parse_cb_ex, ssl, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_add_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_free_cb, ssl, _, _, _);
    ensures normal resource_callback_slot_invoked(ssl, ssl_ctx_st.custom_ext_parse_cb, ssl, _, _, _, _, _);
